{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_017PAUeryTJ4a1L7Udg7UBsE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Anchor R&D Control Surface â€” Master Plan (planning trio session summary)\n\n**Goal / North Star (locked)**\n- Transform Anchor from a task/project tracker into a **per-project R&D control surface**, where each code project is a folder (e.g. `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home`, `C:\\dev\\Anchor`).\n- A single-instance dashboard window drives the **researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman** trio as durable, server-owned Claude Code jobs on gwl-server.\n- Scope of the surface: versioned effort history, taskâ†”project integration, project lifecycle states, deliverable execution, and a data-free public distribution.\n\n**Locked architectural decisions**\n- **D1 â€” One uniform job primitive.** A job is `claude -p --input-format stream-json --output-format stream-json` running the relevant skill (researchPrime / crucible / foreman) in the project cwd, **owned by the Anchor server**. A \"lane\" is just which skill + prompt template; there is no per-lane orchestration code, no PTY, and the implementation stays stdlib-only.\n- **D2 â€” Gate handling is in-session.** A skill's `AskUserQuestion` gate surfaces in the stream (it auto-dismisses headless, but the structured question stays visible); Anchor renders it in a prompt box and sends the user's choice back as a plain text turn to drive continuation.\n\n**Locked user decisions (from the Decision Log, Crucible 2026-06-07/08)**\n- Brownfield **extend of Anchor** (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`); objective = new capability (not a rewrite).\n- Session model = **streaming console, stdlib-only** â€” not a full TUI, no PTY, no dependencies.\n- Registry = a **new parallel R&D registry**, kept distinct from the life-domain projects.\n- Artifacts live **inside each project's `.anchor/`** as pointer-records; the engine's native outputs stay in place.\n- v1 scope = **all three trio lanes, Claude Code CLI only**; Gemini is deferred.\n- Auth = **run the Anchor service as `john`**, resolving the LocalSystem credential wall.\n- Remote access = **bind the Tailscale interface + a shared-secret token** on mutating `/api/*` endpoints.\n\n**Provenance**\n- These claims are grounded in the four member documents of the session: the Master Plan (frozen design), the Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready), the Execution Log, and the Decision Log.\n\n---\nNote: this is the original (v1) Master Plan trio session. The repo's `CLAUDE.md` and memory index show this design was subsequently built and superseded by v2, v3, and v4 (\"Project Cockpit,\" merged to master 2026-06-13) â€” so several v1 decisions (notably \"no PTY\") were later revised (v3+ added the optional `pywinpty` ConPTY terminal). Let me know if you'd like the summary reconciled against the current state rather than the frozen v1 design."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45166,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ebcd91ee-d380-4fe5-aa74-cf9b3035f1e3","uuid":"e2685071-a3a0-4d12-b55d-b680218d8b05","request_id":"req_011Cc1JNSF59oc97QdKDgVE4"}
